<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n90193" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προστρόπ-αιος</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποτιτρόπαιος</span></b>  (<i><span class="en">
			A.
			<u>Supp.</u>
			362
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			<u>Eu.</u>
			176
		</span></i>, both lyr.), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προστροπή</span>) prop. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>turning oneself towards</i>: hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> of one who has incurred pollution by
			committing a crime and <i>turns to a</i>
			<i>god</i> or <i>man to obtain purification, suppliant for
				purification</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν προστρόπαιον, τὸν ἱκέτην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					930
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				362
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Eu.</u>
				234
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				445
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				1173
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Heracl.</u>
				1015
			</span></i>, etc.: as Adj., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕδραν
				ἔχοντα π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				41
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προστρόπαιοι λιταί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OC</u>
					1309
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>suppliant for vengeance</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				286
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ag.</u>
				1587
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				2.3.10
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of one who
			has not yet been purified after committing crime, <i>polluted
				person</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>HF</u>
				1259
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τῆς πόλεως</span>
			<i>bringing pollution</i> on the city, prob. in <i><span class="en">
				Eup.
				120
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὑτοῦ π., μὴ γὰρ δὴ τῆς πόλεως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aeschin.
					2.158
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> of pollution
			incurred, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. αἷμα</span> blood <i>that
				cries for vengeance</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ion</u>
				1260
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>HF</u>
				1161
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδενὶ οὐδὲν π. καταλείψει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antipho
					3.4.9
				</span></i>
			: neut. as Subst., <i>guilt</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προστρόπαιον ἑαυτοῖς προσέθεντο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.C.
					42.3
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			 (= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾧ ἄν τις προστρέποιτο
				δεόμενος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1807.11
			</span></i>), the god <i>to whom the murdered person turns</i> for
			vengeance, <i>avenger</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ τῶν
				θανόντων π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				4.1.4
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				4.2.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				23.10.2
			</span></i> (pl.), <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				2.18.2
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
